<title>BELGIUM: EU says probes British Gas /Group 4 venture.</title>
<headline>EU says probes British Gas /Group 4 venture.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it started a routine probe into a proposed joint venture between British Gas Trading Plc and Group 4 Utility Services Ltd to supply meter reading services in Britain.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement that at first sight the deal could fall under the European Union's merger rules which ban the creation or strengthening of dominant positions in the EU.</p>
<p>Group 4 Utility Services belongs to Group 4 Securitas NV, the statement said. British Gas Trading Plc is a subsidiary of British Gas Plc. The joint venture will be called AccuRead Ltd.</p>
<p>The Commission has about a month to clear the deal or start a full, four-month, investigation.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
</text>
